Added `AIModel.kind`, which records whether a model is for chat or for embedding. A chat model and an embedding model are not interchangeable and are not even the same endpoint, so configuring a retrieval feature with a chat model is now refused before any network traffic instead of becoming a provider-side error later. It defaults to `chat`, so every record that existed before means what it always meant. The Discover AI Models job leaves it at the default, because `GET /v1/models` carries no field it could be read from.
